          "source_title": "Energiewirtschaftsgesetz (EnWG) \u00a7 118(6), gesetze-im-internet.de",
          "source_url": "https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/enwg_2005/__118.html",
          "notes": "Official text: installations for storing electrical energy newly built after 31 December 2008 and commissioned from 4 August 2011 within 18 years (i.e. by 4 August 2029) are exempt for 20 years from commissioning from grid-access charges (Entgelte f\u00fcr den Netzzugang) on energy withdrawn for storage, provided the energy is taken from a transmission or distribution grid and the recovered energy is fed back into the same grid. The exemption does not automatically cover every levy or concession fee. For the illustrative 1 MW / 2 MWh paper asset, assumed commissioned in the exemption window and same-grid, the sourced preset applies 0 \u20ac/MWh grid-access charge on stored energy. This is a legal condition, not a published TSO tariff table."
